{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "One 500 m2 pad-and-vent greenhouse at Tulsa, one strategy, four crop target bands. The equipment is identical in all four scenarios: same geometry, envelope, ventilation, pad, heater, installed fixture power, prices and site, with no mechanical cooling and no dehumidifier anywhere. Only the crop program changes, which is the target band (day and night temperature targets, the VPD window, the dew-point ceiling) together with the daily light target and the leaf area and transpiration assumption that belong to that crop. Leaf area moves with the crop here on purpose, because that is what a user selecting a crop preset gets, but Morris screening ranks leaf area and transpiration as the most influential assumption in this model, so read the spread as the whole crop program and not as the temperature band in isolation. The tomato row is the illustrative preset, not a calibrated tomato water or yield model.",
